course: dictionary
lesson: 16098
title: Wealthy and the wealthy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wealthy means having a lot of money and property. It is another word for rich. Read the words around it to check: «The wealthy family owned three houses and a big boat» tells you they had lots of money and things.
explain: Wealthy can also be a noun when you put the in front of it. «The wealthy» means rich people as a group. «The wealthy often live in big houses» is talking about rich people in general, not one person.
explain: Wealthy has forms for comparing: wealthy, wealthier, wealthiest. «The baker was wealthy, the mayor was wealthier, and the lord was the wealthiest in the town» puts three people in order from less rich to most rich.
fact: Wealthy means having a lot of money and property; it means rich.
fact: «The wealthy» means rich people as a group.
fact: Wealthy, wealthier, wealthiest help you compare how rich people are.
fact: «A wealthy merchant sold silk in the old market.»
fact: Books about history and social studies often describe the difference between wealthy and poor people.
exercise: «The wealthy family owned three houses and a big boat.» What does wealthy mean? | Very old | Poor and hungry | *Having a lot of money and property | Lost at sea
exercise: «The wealthy often live in big houses.» In this sentence, what does «the wealthy» mean? | *Rich people as a group | People who work in a shop | Stone walls | One lonely person
exercise: Sara is ___ than Ben, who has only one coin. Which word fits the gap? | wealth | wealthily | *wealthier | poorest
test: «The merchant was wealthy, so he bought a golden ship.» Which word is closest in meaning to wealthy? | Brave | Hungry | *Rich | Tired
test: Which sentence uses «the wealthy» to mean rich people as a group? | I found a wealthy coin under the rug. | *The wealthy of the town gave a big party. | The wealthy man walked his dog.
exam: Which word means the same as wealthy? | Quiet | *Rich | Hungry | Tiny
